# The FMLA leave an employee has left in a 12-month period. It counts minutes because 825.205(a)(1) allows
# an employer no increment over one hour, and lets it use a shorter one: minutes hold them all. The period
# is a name the employer gives it, for the first three of the methods of 825.200(b). The fourth, a 12-month
# period measured backward from each day of leave, moves every day and needs another shape.
book fmla_leave v1
description "The FMLA leave an employee has left in a 12-month period, in minutes: it starts at what the employee is entitled to, and a designation holds what will be taken"

unit min

account leave(employee: string, period: string) : min
  description "what is left of the 12 or 26 workweeks of 29 CFR 825.200"
  at least 0 refused as not_enough_leave
account entitled : min outside
  description "where what an employee is entitled to comes from"
account taken : min outside
  description "where the leave goes once it is taken"

transfer entitle(employee: string, period: string, minutes: min)
  description "what the employee is entitled to in the period, from the rule fmla_entitlement"
  key employee, period
  move minutes from entitled to leave(employee, period)

transfer designate(request: string, employee: string, period: string, minutes: min)
  description "held while the leave is designated: posted when it is taken, voided when it is not"
  key request
  pending never expires
  move minutes from leave(employee, period) to taken
